 from a pool of 3,985 applicants, the awarded artists are all based in New York and range in age from 25 to 90. The NYSCA/NYFA program also announced 16 finalists, who will receive NYFA services and unrestricted cash grants of $1,000. Artists Melissa Joseph , Hakan Topal , Jeffrey Meris, and Sabri Sundos are among the many recipients and finalists. Prevailing interests in cultural expression and the environment emerged across disciplines this year, from references to Korean burial traditions to sculptures compiled out of wood, salmon skin, and beeswax thread. In the digital and electronic arts category, fellows also mingled their artworks with explorations of AI and technological advancements, with panelists observing "increasingly blurred boundaries between traditional discipline categories" in a July 23 announcement. Craft/Sculpture recipient Sasha Fishman's "I want to be wet" (2024) (photo by Josh Schaedel) The 2027 award cycle opens in the fall of 2026 , with eligible proposals in: fiction; folk and traditional arts; interdisciplinary work; painting; and video and film. Below is a list of all the fellows and finalists of the 2026 NYSCA/NYFA Artist Fellowship in the visual arts categories. Craft/Sculpture Recipients Paria Ahmadi (New York) Patricia Encarnacion (Bronx) julien feller (Essex) Aaron Feltman (Ulster) Sasha Fishman (Kings) Danielle Gadus (Kings) Covey Gong (New York) JesÃºs Hilario-Reyes (Kings) Alex Ito (Queens) Paloma Izquierdo (Kings) Emily Janowick (Queens) Melissa Joseph (Kings) Tamiko Kawata (New York) Catherine Telford Keogh (New York) Ellie Krakow (New York) Megan Mi-Ai Lee (New York) Chico MacMurtrie (Kings) Jeffrey Meris (New York) Kristyna and Marek Milde (Kings) Anna Ting MÃ¶ller (Kings) Brian Oakes (Kings) Saman & Sasan Oskouei (Queens) Chelsey Pettyjohn (Kings) Vartan Poghosian (Oneida) Lina Puerta (New York) lucÃ­a reissig (Kings) Alvaro Villa (Westchester) Patrice Renee Washington (Orange) Anne Wu (Queens) JAYOUNG YOON (Dutchess) Craft/